# ligand_library_builder -- where the software lives on this machine.
#
# Site layout: one directory per cluster, never in ~, with the checkout inside
# it. llb finds hpc.env as ../hpc.env from its checkout:
#   $LLB_SITE/ligand_library_builder/     the checkout
#   $LLB_SITE/hpc.env                     this file: cluster settings, shared by the site's users
#   $LLB_SITE/users/$USER.env             per-user keys, read after hpc.env
#   cp config/hpc.env.example ../hpc.env
#
# Per-user keys go in users/$USER.env (same syntax), not here, so one hpc.env
# serves everyone: LLB_ACCOUNT when yours differs, your own ZINC_DATA. Anything
# set there overrides this file.
#
# Lookup order (common/env.sh llb_load_config); the old places still work:
#   LLB_CONFIG=/path/to/hpc.env     an override; nothing else is tried
#   ../hpc.env                      the site layout
#   config/hpc.env                  inside the checkout (gitignored)
# users/$USER.env is looked for beside whichever hpc.env is used.
#
# Every wrapper and SLURM script reads the config through common/env.sh.
# Nothing else in the repo hard-codes a path to a tool, so this file is the
# only one to edit when moving machines.
#
# Plain bash: KEY=value, no spaces around '='. Empty means "use the default".
#
# Each tool (PREP, DOCK) has up to three knobs, applied in this order:
#   <TOOL>_SETUP  shell run BEFORE conda activation (`module purge`, `module load ...`)
#   <TOOL>_ENV    conda env to activate: a name, or an absolute prefix path.
#   <TOOL>_EXE    explicit executable, when it is not on PATH inside the env.
#
# Download, sampling and `llb chunk` need only the system python3 and SLURM.

# ---- conda -------------------------------------------------------------------
# Resolved BEFORE any setup hook runs, so a `module purge` cannot hide it.
# Empty = `conda info --base`. Great Lakes: /nfs/turbo/umms-maom/johnbick/miniforge3
CONDA_BASE=

# ---- SLURM -------------------------------------------------------------------
LLB_ACCOUNT=maom99
LLB_PARTITION=standard
# Max simultaneously running array tasks (sbatch --array=...%N), per array:
# llb chunk's collect array and llb zinc3d-extract.
LLB_ARRAY_PARALLEL=50

# ---- download (mol_download/) --------------------------------------------------
# Where the ~1 TB of 2D SMILES goes (scratch, not home). run.sh mirrors the URL
# path under it: $ZINC_DATA/zinc22/2d/H17/H17M100.smi.gz
ZINC_DATA=
WGET=wget
PARALLEL=parallel

# ---- PREP: Python with RDKit and pandas (environments/llb.yml) -----------------
# llb mol2-library, llb collapse-invertomers and the zinc3d-* steps.
PREP_SETUP=""
PREP_ENV=llb

# ---- DOCK6 / db2tool (dock6_claude, pinned 294d235) ---------------------------
# Only for docking/db2_to_mol2.py (mol2 from the db2). A compiled binary, so
# no conda env: DOCK_SETUP loads whatever it was built against (module load ...).
DOCK_SETUP=""
DOCK_ENV=
# Empty = `db2tool` on PATH after DOCK_SETUP.
DB2TOOL_EXE=
